Z||000015||ChadMan||12-08-2000||11:38 AM||||Hey, wasn't there a 2000GT in the James Bond flick "You Only Live Twice"?  <P>If I remember right, Bond was strolling along about to be ambushed and shot when this beautiful Japanese girl came tooling along and yelled for Bond to jump in, saving his skin.<P>I find it disturbing when people say Japanese cars/bikes have no heritage, soul, spirit, etc.  Read up on Soichiro Honda, then tell me Hondas have no heritage.<P>I just happen to have a greater appreciation for American automotive heritage, that's all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000016||FieroSTETZ||12-10-2000||12:54 PM||||my family helped to sell a 77 celica gt for my uncle when he got cancer (hes better now) that was a fun car! at one point, i was deciding between getting my gt or the celica. inside, its tiny- yet not uncomfortable, and its got that great 22r engine! things run forever. my girlfriend's dad has a 74 toyota pickup with 380k and change on the clock, and it doesnt leak, doesnt burn oil, and ist still pretty peppy- plus, there is a plethora of mods for the 22r, f/e theres a website selling carbeurated 22r's with 245 hp... from 2.2 litres!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
